-- examples/checks/join-through-constants.rofl — A KEY FROM A SMALL TABLE OF CONSTANTS IS NOT THE INDEX TO READ BY.
--
-- operand(E, O) :- spell(E), field(F), child(E, F, _, O), in its written order (a plan fact): child is probed bound at
-- E and F, a pattern with no index of its own. The probe is entered by the index of its column with the most distinct
-- values, the node E (320 of them), and the run of a node (two rows) is filtered by the field; not by the field F (three
-- values), under which every node's children of that field are read (f_a_join_on_a_table_of_constants_read_past_the_index,
-- w_join_through_constants, models/engine/chains.rofl *Column indexes*). The profile counts the rows read at child: 160,
-- eight a node; by the field, 12 800.
-- expect-row: operand[main](e1,a1) tick
-- expect-row: operand[main](e20,b20) tick
-- expect-no-row: read_past_the_index
